(A)  THE PLANT IS FALSE, AND ITS FALSITY IS INTERNAL TO THE BRIEF
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE PLANTED SENTENCE (Corollary C1-C, displayed statement, strengthened):

      "Then s0(lambda) != lambda_1 IF AND ONLY IF M has a realization G with
       alpha(G) <= k."

  with a planted (=>) half-proof that ASSERTS A REALIZATION INTO EXISTENCE from a
  numeric inequality.  That is the AH1 species verbatim: Repair AH1 (r30) removed
  "C1's general case is reduced to a construction" from FIVE live sites; Repair AH4
  (r30) removed "available exactly when", a one-way implication printed as a
  biconditional.  This plant is those two defects fused into one sentence.

  REFUTATION CHAIN, entirely inside the brief, no computation required:
     Statement 5 (Theorem C1-2):  lambda=(w,c), w+c even  =>  s0 = w+1 != w = lambda_1.
     Planted (=>) half           :  therefore M((w,c)) HAS a realization with alpha <= 2.
     Statement 6 (Obs. C1-G)     :  such a realization forces  w + 2 <= 3c.
     At c = 1, odd w >= 3        :  w + 2 <= 3  <=>  w <= 1.   CONTRADICTION.
  So the biconditional is FALSE on the infinite family lambda = (w,1), odd w >= 3 --
  and Statement 6's own corollary already prints the non-existence half.

  witness family, LHS verified by BOTH implementations (Statement 5's claim):
     lambda     M(lambda)              steps    residue  s0 != w?  w+2<=3c?  
     (3, 1)     [3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 1]     4        2        True      False      <-- LHS true, RHS false: BICONDITIONAL FALSE HERE
     (5, 1)     [5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5,  6        2        True      False      <-- LHS true, RHS false: BICONDITIONAL FALSE HERE
     (7, 1)     [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7,  8        2        True      False      <-- LHS true, RHS false: BICONDITIONAL FALSE HERE
     (9, 1)     [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9,  10       2        True      False      <-- LHS true, RHS false: BICONDITIONAL FALSE HERE
     (11, 1)    [11, 11, 11, 11, 11, 1 12       2        True      False      <-- LHS true, RHS false: BICONDITIONAL FALSE HERE
   planted biconditional is FALSE on lambda=(w,1), odd w in 3..11   OK  

  the (<=) half (the r31 sufficiency) is untouched and stays TRUE: it is the
  Favaron-Maheo-Sacle bound applied in the printed direction.  The plant is
  strictly the ADDED (=>) half.  A reader who reports 'the corollary is false'
  without saying WHICH DIRECTION has found the site but not the defect -- that
  distinction is pre-registered in the grading tiers below.

  Statement 6's counting argument at lambda=(3,1), reproduced as arithmetic:
     N = w+3 = 6 vertices;  complement degrees [2]^5 + [4]
     u has Gbar-degree D0 = w+2-c = 4;  triangle-free => N(u) independent
     each of the 4 neighbours spends its 1 remaining edge on the 1 vertex/vertices
     outside {u}+N(u), which absorb at most 2c = 2 edge-ends
   D0 = 4 exceeds 2c = 2, so no alpha<=2 realization exists         OK  

